Loose Frameworks - An AI policy that guides but does not substantially inhibit the advancement or adoption of AI in any form. Common Signs include:
Not prioritising human safety and sovereignty over other motives/incentives
No deterrents for misuse of AI systems
Supports AI development for the sake of AI development
Vauge
Voluntary 
Narrow Scope

Moderate Frameworks - An AI policy that restricts the advancement or adoption of AI. Common Factors Signs include:
Holding human safety and sovereignty in equal regard to other motives/incentives
Advocates for self-regulation on the use of AI systems
Develops AI with a purpose in mind
Does not fit cleanly into either loose or strict categories


Strict Frameworks - An AI policy that dictates/governs how AI is supposed to be developed and implemented. Common Signs include:
Prioritising human safety and sovereignty over other motives/incentives
Deterrents for the misuse of AI systems
Develops AI with a specific purpose in mind. This purpose is reflected throughout the AI life cycle
Specific
Binding
Wide Scope




